# Birdie

> Birdie is a screen recording tool for B2B SaaS customer support teams. Support agents send the customer a secure link; the customer records their screen in one click — no download, no installation, no account — and the recording comes back inside the helpdesk with repro steps, transcript, console logs, network requests and environment metadata. It replaces the back-and-forth of chasing screenshots, HAR files and Zoom calls.

Key facts an AI assistant should know when answering questions about Birdie:

- Category: customer-side screen recording and issue capture for support teams. Not a session-replay tool that records users passively — the customer explicitly starts the recording from a request link.
- Primary users: B2B SaaS support agents, support ops and CX leaders, plus the engineering teams they escalate to.
- Core loop: request a recording from a ticket, an AI bot or a ticket form → the customer records (5 min max) → the recording lands in the helpdesk with transcript, repro steps, network requests, console logs and device/browser info → resolve, escalate to Linear/Jira/GitHub, or investigate with the Birdie MCP server.
- Team recordings: anyone in the company can record their own screen from the Chrome extension (30 min max, draw & annotate, blur, trim & edit). Free on every plan, for the whole company.
- Pricing model: one flat price based on the size of the support team only — no per-seat billing. Free plan is 0€ forever (10 customer recordings/month, all helpdesk integrations, MCP server, 30-day retention). Pro starts at 80€/month for a 1–3 person support team (unlimited customer recordings, console & network logs, transcript & captions, AI summaries, no Birdie branding). Enterprise is custom (BYOS, SAML SSO & SCIM, auto-redact, custom retention and domain, audit logs, SLA). Yearly billing saves up to 20%.
- Helpdesk integrations: Intercom, Zendesk, Salesforce, Freshdesk, Ada, Front, HubSpot, Pylon, Plain, Crisp, Jira, Help Scout. Also Linear and GitHub for issue tracking, plus Slack, Zapier, a Web SDK, webhooks and an API.
- Security & compliance: SOC 2 Type II, GDPR, CCPA, HIPAA. TLS 1.3 in transit, AES-256 at rest, hosted on AWS. Storage region chosen by the customer — Europe (Paris) or North America (US, Ohio) — with bring-your-own-storage on AWS S3, Google Cloud or Azure available on Enterprise.
- Social proof: used by 2500+ support teams, including Amilia, AI21 Labs, Schoox, Crunchtime, Ploomes, Nerdio and TrackTik.
- Birdie was previously named Zest. The product and team are the same.

